[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1548","stub":{"id":"1548","section":"1. Sheep Creek Rd to Green Peter Reservoir","altname":"","river":"Santiam, Middle","difficulty":"IIItoIVstandoutV","states":["USA-ORE"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"1.87","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:10:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"levelFT","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"107974","location":{"latitude":"44.466999","longitude":"-122.147003"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"113217","location":{"latitude":"44.505001","longitude":"-122.387001"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"15.5","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"887009","ext":"png","post_id":"889751","description":"This was the flow for this trip report\r\nhttp://mthoodh2o.blogspot.com/2014/09/marathon-on-middle.html\r\n\r\nThis was minimum for the upper put in, and more reasonable (but still low) for the lower put in.","caption":"Gauge","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/887009","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/887009"}},{"id":"887015","ext":"png","post_id":"889757","description":"This maps shows the hiking routes if you are using the lower put in.","caption":"Lower Put ins","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/887015","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/887015"}},{"id":"891605","ext":"jpg","post_id":"895491","description":null,"caption":" on Santiam, Middle @1. Sheep Creek Rd to Green Peter Reservoir","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/891605","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/891605"}},{"id":"892619","ext":"jpg","post_id":"896475","description":null,"caption":" on Santiam, Middle @1. Sheep Creek Rd to Green Peter Reservoir","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/892619","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/892619"}}],"detail":{"id":"1548","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"**Gauge:**  The gauge only reads in feet, and this section is not commonly done so data points are few.  That said, after a handful of recent trips the consensus seems to be 4-4.5 feet is the goldilocks level, not too high, not too low.  Runs just under 4' were still considered worthwhile, and a run at 3.5' and dropping slowly was considered worth doing if you've not done it before.   If you do the run please report in the comments. If flows are below 3.5' use the lower put in unless you are ok with scraping.   A group who camped at the put in bailed when they woke to flows spiking over 5' and there were no eddies to be seen.  Yet another local paddler did the run while it was dropping from 5.2-5.0 and felt the level was a perfect medium-high.\n\nHere is a link showing **[inflow to Green Peter Reservoir](http://www.nwd-wc.usace.army.mil/dd/common/projects/www/gpr.html)**, if you subtract the **[Quartzville flow](http://waterdata.usgs.gov/usa/nwis/uv?14185900)** it is possible to get a ballpark on what is flowing down the Middle Santiam.\n\nThis is a unique and remote wilderness run in the heart of Oregon's Cascades.  The first day is shorter than the second, with a creeky feel and a few scouts.  Just below the put in bridge is the OK Coral, a class V-ish gorge, that some paddlers will choose to put in below that by working their way down Lake Creek, or bushwhacking in off a road on river left.  This small road heads towards Holman Creek from the main shuttle road less than half a mile upstream of the put in bridge.   The rest of the first day is fun read and run III-IV with the exception of Geomorph, a landslide rapid scouted and portaged right, and Shelter Falls at the confluence with Bachelor Creek.  The Shelter Shedd is on river left in the vicinity of the powerful, short Shelter Falls.  Intermediate paddlers will enjoy this upper section by putting in below the OK Coral, and portaging around the two larger rapids. As always, keep an eye out for wood, and don't be surprised by a portage or two (though often the wood situation requires no portaging).\n\nThe best camping is in the mile downstream of Pyramid Creek, with the very best near Donaca Creek.\n\nThe second day has long stretches of quality read and run class III/IV rapids separated by easy floating.  The scenery is an interesting contrast between old growth wilderness and clear cuts exposing large cliff walls.  The whitewater is non-descript boulder gardens, but lots of fun and people tend to be surprised by the amount of quality rapids on the run.\n\nPaddling this run (especially as an overnight trip) should be on the bucket list of any Oregonian paddler.\n\nThere is a shelter early on in the run that opens up the run to foul weather overnights.  The better camping is near Donaca Creek, on big open gravel and moss bars.\n\nDetailed information in a **[Trip Report](http://mthoodh2o.blogspot.com/2014/09/marathon-on-middle.html)** from Into the Outside.\n\n**Take Out:**  Whitcomb Creek Park.  This park has a boat ramp that is the conventional take out.  It is six miles of paddling along the reservoir to reach this take out.\n\n**Put In**:  Return to Hwy 20 and drive east about 24 miles to NF 2047/Sheep Creek Rd where you turn left.  Follow this road 8.7 miles to a bridge over the Middle Santiam (stay right at 0.3, left at 0.4, center/main at 2.3, right but not hard right at 3.6, then stay left just after, right at 5.9, 7.9 and 8.4).\n\nA shorter section requiring a hike in is described **[here](http://www.oregonkayaking.net/tales/somewhere_in_the_middle/somewhere_in_the_middle.html)**.  This lower option also allows for lower water trips, even below 3.5'.\n\nThe directions for putting in lower are described **[here](http://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/willamette/recarea/?recid=81014)**, both options described on that page work for boating.  The first option puts you in near Shedd Camp Shelter and the second further downstream near the confluence with Pyramid Creek.","averageGradient":"60","maxGradient":null,"length":"17.9","correlations":[{"reachID":"1548","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"levelFT","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"3","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"5.5"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"MIDDLE SANTIAM R NEAR CASCADIA, OR","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"14185800","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":null,"latestStageReading":{"value":"1.87","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:10:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"44.5151239","longitude":"-122.3720249"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/14185800","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/14185800/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":"Previous Flowbands: \nLow Runnable Range (R0-R5): 3 - 3.5 levelFT  Comment: Use lower put in\nRange of Boatable Flows (R0-R9): 3.5 - 5.5 levelFT  Comment: \n\nMigration Errors: \nDifferent ranges are defining the same values","comment":null,"status":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading